# CALIB keywords, PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 3.2 (macos 2026-10-11).
# tst_calib_opttol.in sets the cap as OptMxItrs= 6 -- the 9-char spelling the parser's 10-char
# 'OptMaxItrs' match missed, so the cap silently stayed at the default 10 -- and the tolerance
# as OptTol= 1e-9, which had no keyword at all.  Both were dropped SILENTLY (no message).  The
# CALIB banner prints the values in force, and the run honours the cap of 6.  The second deck
# declares no OptTol: the per-load default 1e-12 comes back (a per-load value, not session
# state).  Pre-fix, measured: no banner, and the opttol deck ran 8 iterations (the default cap
# of 10, the old loop's 0.7T exit) -- red.
old $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/tst_calib_opttol.in
calib
no
no
old $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/tst_calib_spot4.in
calib
no
no
# EXPECT: tst_calib_opttol\.in\s+being loaded[\s\S]*?LM stop: OptTol \(abs rms\) =\s+1\.000E-09\s+OptMaxItrs =\s+6\s
# EXPECT: tst_calib_opttol\.in\s+being loaded[\s\S]*?Optimization iterations =\s+6\s[\s\S]*?tst_calib_spot4\.in\s+being loaded
# EXPECT: tst_calib_spot4\.in\s+being loaded[\s\S]*?LM stop: OptTol \(abs rms\) =\s+1\.000E-12\s+OptMaxItrs =\s+4\s
# EXPECT-NOT: Unidentified string\s*=\s*Opt
